<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tacfarinas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 24 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tacfarinas was a Numidian of the Musulamii who had served in the Roman auxiliary army and from 17 CE led a revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> tactics, he drew in the Gaetuli and Moorish groups and resisted several Roman commanders for seven years. He was killed in 24 CE in a surprise attack led by the proconsul Publius Cornelius Dolabella.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tacfarinas.jpg" alt="Tacfarinas" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hynox.qualaty · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mausolee_Takfarinas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
